      "title": "chiefly of *Plocamium pacificum*, and other red algae. In comparison, the four Hawaiian habitats were characterized as: 1) a protected reef habitat, which was dominated by a variety of massive and branching stony corals, mostly *Porites* spp.; 2) a boulder habitat, where the major biological features were encrusting corals, especially *Porites lobata*, and isolated heads of *Pocillopora meandrina*; and 4) an outer drop-off habitat that was dominated by fields of branching corals, mostly *Porites compressa*. These predominating biological features, both warm-temperate and tropical, were strongly influenced by three variables: nature of the underlying substrate, water depth, and relative exposure to wave surge.",
